  'yTerm': 'Do you want to go for a walk?\nDo you want to sit in a chair?\nI\'m going to grab a coworker and we\'ll help you\nDo you want to get back in bed?\nWe can walk down the hallway together\nHold my hand\nI\'ll help you\nWait for me\nI\'ll be right back\n\nPhysical Therapy / PT: in ICU setting, comes during daytime primarily on weekdays; helps ""mobilize"" patients / the team helps figure out which assistive devices (canes, walker, etc) are most appropriate for people to get out of bed with. If someone has been sedated / unconscious for a while, we typically wait until PT comes to get them out of bed for the first time, if their muscles are deconditioned / if they haven\'t used their muscles in a while',
